  "normalized_load_bearing_statements": [
    {
      "characters": 586,
      "name": "CIRCDIST.gross.claim",
      "sha256": "fc22f602b9bfd9e38fa69d7fc1d00b973c7a634e6c400662eaccd38c8ec0f180",
      "text": "For the Gross code [[144,12,12]] with single-ancilla CNOT syndrome extraction (interleaving of X- and Z-check CNOTs allowed; each required CNOT exactly once; one two-qubit gate per qubit per time step; no flag ancillas, cat states, or generating-set changes; idle layers compressed), the optimum D*_Gross = max over legal schedules M of d_circ(C(M)) is determined with proof, as either an explicit interleaved schedule with certified d_circ = 12, or a proof that every legal schedule satisfies d_circ <= 11; and the published conjectured distance-11 circuit has a certified d_circ = 11."
    },
    {
      "characters": 300,
      "name": "candidate-certification.implication",
      "sha256": "4f40673227208c58d21650b3d685670019f5460b44ee52c0440b22293eec1598",
      "text": "Via SBB26 Thm 1 the statement d_circ = 11 for the candidate circuit reduces to an exact minimum-distance certification on a 360-column extended code (not a circuit-level DEM search); combined with the universal d_ext cap this certifies the first half of the claim and pins the achievable floor at 11."
    },
    {
      "characters": 279,
      "name": "gap-via-lift.implication",
      "sha256": "915109fe708c63ce138b11d07aa87c3048d676c87d9d6b7a80d68c0e2025c5d1",
      "text": "Given the universal d_ext <= 11 cap, D* = 12 holds iff some interleaved schedule has completion gap >= 1 at weight 12; the closed-lift criterion turns this into a voltage/monodromy condition checkable per witness family, deciding the second half of the claim in either direction."
    }
  ],
